All,
The design of HDPE caps utilizing a plate or puck machined from sheet stock=
 have been qualified under testing to ASTM F2206 and FM1613 and confirmed w=
ith regular testing to C906 and FM1613.  The following guidelines should in=
form your pricing and/or manufacturing and should not be deviated from with=
out consulting with Product Engineering.

Molded caps, if available, are not part of the below considerations.

DR7 & DR9
In sizes 2"-6" the sheet stock to be machined will be 3" thick.
In sizes 8"-18" the sheet stock will be 4" thick.
In sizes over 18" swage reducers should be used to reduce to 18" at which p=
oint a cap from 4" thick material can be fused on.

DR11 and thinner
In sizes 2"-12" the sheet stock to be machined will be 3" thick.
In sizes 14"-24" the sheet stock will be 4" thick.
In sizes over 24" swage reducers should be used to reduce to 24" at which p=
oint a cap from 4" thick material can be fused on.


--_000_7e148fdf15b04245aa85d2a48d3c059aharcofittingscom_
